# Build context filter for `docker build` (and docker-compose build:).
#
# Anything matched here is invisible to the Docker daemon, so the broad
# `COPY app/ ./app/` and `COPY scripts/ ./scripts/` in Dockerfile won't
# accidentally bundle developer-only or sensitive paths into the image.

# --- DEV-FIXTURES (the reason this file exists) ----------------------------
# scripts/dev-fixtures/ ships site-specific seeders + topology templates
# (e.g. caict_v4.py). PR #5's stated invariant is that *commercial code
# carries zero topology templates* — operators on a fresh image must build
# their topology in the GUI editor. Without this exclusion, the Dockerfile's
# `COPY scripts/ ./scripts/` brings dev-fixtures into the image and
# `GET /switch-topologies/templates` would surface CAICT to every customer.
scripts/dev-fixtures/

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# .env contains DATABASE_URL with credentials. Production should inject
# this via docker-compose `environment:` / orchestrator secrets, not bake
# it into the image. .env.example is safe (it's a template) but excluded
# for consistency.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- Python build hygiene ---------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Local virtualenv -------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/

# --- Stale dev SQLite artifacts ---------------------------------------------
# Container talks to Postgres via DATABASE_URL; these are leftovers from
# test runs that pollute the image and confuse newcomers.
*.db
*.db.bak
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Dev logs ---------------------------------------------------------------
logs/

# --- Tests ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed at runtime; CI runs pytest outside the production image.
tests/

# --- Git / editor metadata --------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
